From 96562d72de5a43b56b8421f821462b0574bb4f63 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 04:04:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ci: fail when the committed route tree is stale

The 2026-08-21 red build came from src/routeTree.gen.ts not being
regenerated after PR #14 added three API routes. Nothing in the pipeline
could catch it: type-check is the step that fails, and it runs before the
build that would regenerate the file.

The production build already regenerates the route tree, so a diff after
it is proof the committed copy was out of date. Assert that, with an
error message naming the fix.

Verified both ways locally: clean tree passes, a one-line edit fails.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QGy3NZWndBAVM8qKdAzXm1
---
 .github/workflows/ci.yml | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/.github/workflows/ci.yml b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
index 211c5eb..12c3de0 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/ci.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
@@ -40,6 +40,19 @@ jobs:
           VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY: ci-placeholder
           VITE_APP_URL: http://localhost:3001
 
+      # A stale committed route tree is exactly what turned CI red on
+      # 2026-08-21: PR #14 added three API routes without regenerating it, and
+      # type-check can never self-heal because it runs BEFORE the build. The
+      # build above regenerates the tree, so any diff here proves the committed
+      # file was out of date.
+      - name: Route tree is up to date
+        run: |
+          if ! git diff --quiet -- src/routeTree.gen.ts; then
+            echo "::error file=src/routeTree.gen.ts::Stale route tree. Run 'npm run build' and commit the regenerated src/routeTree.gen.ts."
+            git diff --stat -- src/routeTree.gen.ts
+            exit 1
+          fi
+
       # Boot the built server and assert the SAFETY invariants: auth is
       # enforced, unsigned Stripe webhooks are rejected, errors leak nothing.
       # Placeholders are enough because every check asserts a REJECTION.
